1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,739
A thin slice crosses the whole path from real-
shaped input to usable output while keeping

2
00:00:05,809 --> 00:00:13,446
scope small. In the course prototype, a ticket enters
a local API, validation checks it, a deterministic

3
00:00:13,516 --> 00:00:18,977
rule suggests a queue, the reviewer inspects
the reason, and an event records the result.

4
00:00:19,047 --> 00:00:22,631
We start with rules to establish
an understandable baseline.

5
00:00:22,701 --> 00:00:29,293
An optional model must later justify its additional
value and risk on the same evaluation set.

6
00:00:29,363 --> 00:00:34,675
The prototype is a teaching system, with
synthetic data and explicit human review.

7
00:00:34,745 --> 00:00:40,463
An architecture diagram with five services
tests no operating assumption by itself.

8
00:00:40,533 --> 00:00:45,845
One ticket appearing on the review screen
tests integration and usability, even if the

9
00:00:45,915 --> 00:00:48,453
implementation has only one service.

10
00:00:48,523 --> 00:00:53,302
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

11
00:00:53,372 --> 00:00:55,356
Run the lab with Docker Compose.

12
00:00:55,426 --> 00:01:01,698
Open the review screen and trace ticket
T001 through input, rule, output, and event.

13
00:01:01,768 --> 00:01:08,488
The complete path uses POST /api/triage, returns
a suggestion with human_review_required set

14
00:01:08,558 --> 00:01:11,011
to true, and writes a suggestion event.

15
00:01:11,081 --> 00:01:15,455
Saving an accepted or overridden
decision produces a separate event.

16
00:01:15,525 --> 00:01:19,023
Inspect both rather than
treating generation as adoption.

17
00:01:19,093 --> 00:01:24,725
GET /health confirms availability, but does
not prove authorized routing or workflow

18
00:01:24,795 --> 00:01:25,926
usefulness.

19
00:01:25,996 --> 00:01:27,681
What makes the slice complete?

20
00:01:27,751 --> 00:01:29,394
A. Many services B.

21
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:31,939
A working input-to-reviewed-output path C.

22
00:01:32,009 --> 00:01:34,163
An attractive architecture diagram.

23
00:01:34,233 --> 00:01:35,705
The best answer is B.

24
00:01:35,775 --> 00:01:39,829
Completeness concerns the value
path, while thinness concerns scope.
